linux-cpupower for Debian
-------------------------

The linux-cpupower package ships a cpupower systemd service unit which is
not enabled and started by default (with a configuration file in
/etc/cpupower-service.conf).

If you want to use the the systemd service enable it with:

  systemctl enable cpupower.service
  systemctl start cpupower.service

 -- Salvatore Bonaccorso <carnil@debian.org>  Mon, 13 Oct 2025 13:54:13 +0200
